<title>USA: Venus Exploration begins SmallCap trading.</title>
<headline>Venus Exploration begins SmallCap trading.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venus Exploration Inc, created by the previously announced merger of the independent oil and gas producer Venus Exploration Inc and Xplor Corp, began trading on June 6 on the Nasdaq SmallCap Exchange under the symbol VENX.O.</p>
<p>The new company is active in development drilling in 11 oil and gas fields and has estimated proved reserves of 11,160 million cubic feet gas equivalent.</p>
<p>The new Venus said it starts with approximately $13.5 million in total book assets and $3 million in working capital.</p>
<p>The new Venus is an oil and gas exploration, development and production company.</p>
</text>
